CommitDate: Mon Nov 2 22:56:19 2026 +0700

    fix(yang.clojure): the intra-unit call lane — both blocked kernel fixtures complete inside the 2M budget
    
    The two blocked fixtures (check-accepted, check-assume-have-discharge)
    exhausted the 2,000,000-step budget because every intra-unit source call
    paid the full common-invocation price: record construction, entry
    dispatch, outcome conversion and bridge capture for a callee the
    compiler statically knew was its own defn. The call entry now carries a
    private second lane - the entry closure takes [invocation direct?] and a
    truthy direct? dispatches the argument vector straight to the body -
    and statically intra-unit calls (top-level defn/defn- symbols, unshadowed,
    never def/defmacro, no external macros active) compile to a
    dsg__intra_call preamble helper that applies the entry with [args true].
    Anything not provably intra-unit keeps the admission-checked path; the
    admission witness check got stricter (the witness must itself be
    callable); dsg__assoc avoids a program-shadowed assoc.
    
    The harness exhaustion ex-data now carries :consumer v (the advanced VM)
    with a regression proving it. Diagnostic evidence from the H3-1 packet;
    zero coverage credit claimed for diagnostics.
    
    Verified after the agy round's quota death, by the seat: both blocked
    fixtures complete and pass - gate counts {pass 102, recorded-deviation
    2, recorded-upstream-failure 2, blocked 0}; the refreshed evidence's
    unexercised set drops 58 -> 20 (the fix re-exercises the 38 arities the
    broken routing had un-credited; 145/165 credited); the focused gate test
    shows exactly one failure (the by-design blocked assertion at 20
    unexercised); the full oracle namespace 26 tests / 1895 assertions with
    the same single failure; yang.base 124/0 (two new regressions included);
    kondo 0/0. Authored by agy (Gemini 4 Argon High); verification completed
    by the seat after agy's quota exhaustion.
