{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_pBAQtBwgHxoxaaR0bZLPADFC","content":"1040\t(defn- check-av-params!\n1041\t  [params]\n1042\t  (when-not (vector? params)\n1043\t    (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params params}))\n1044\t  (doseq [p params]\n1045\t    (when (= '& p)\n1046\t      (reject! \"Variadic fn parameters are not supported\" {:params params}))\n1047\t    (check-binder! p params)))\n1048\t\n1049\t\n1050\t(defn- outcome-node\n1051\t  [tag value]\n1052\t  (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/lit tag)) value))\n1053\t\n1054\t\n1055\t(defn- call-entry\n1056\t  \"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body.\n1057\t   A truthy second argument selects the unit's private intra-unit lane,\n1058\t   where `invocation` is already the positional argument vector.\"\n1059\t  []\n1060\t  (let [body (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"body\"))\n1061\t        invocation (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invocation\"))\n1062\t        direct? (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"direct\"))\n1063\t        outcome (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"entry_outcome\"))\n1064\t        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n1065\t        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n1066\t        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n1067\t        binding-error (outcome-node\n1068\t                        error-tag\n1069\t                        (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1070\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/message)\n1071\t                               (u/lit \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\")\n1072\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/data)\n1073\t                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1074\t                                      (u/lit :yang.call/named) named)))\n1075\t        entry-body (u/let1\n1076\t                     outcome\n1077\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1078\t                                (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1079\t                                binding-error)\n1080\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1081\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 0))\n1082\t                                       (u/lit ok-tag))\n1083\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))\n1084\t                                (u/app raise\n1085\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/thrown)\n1086\t                                              (u/app (u/v 'data/nth)\n1087\t                                                     (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))))))\n1088\t        ;; The private lanes forward the body's outcome in tail position.\n1089\t        ;; The public 1-arg entry nil-fills `direct?` and converts outcomes\n1090\t        ;; to value/raise normally unless authenticated by `:clj/outcome-token`.\n1091\t        entry (u/lam [invocation direct?]\n1092\t                     (u/if-node\n1093\t                       (u/v direct?)\n1094\t                       (u/app (u/v body) (u/v invocation))\n1095\t                       (u/if-node\n1096\t                         (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1097\t                                (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation)\n1098\t                                       (u/lit :clj/outcome-token))\n1099\t                                (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1100\t                         (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1101\t                                    (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1102\t                                    binding-error)\n1103\t                         entry-body)))]\n1104\t    (u/lam [body] entry)))\n1105\t\n1106\t\n1107\t(defn- admit-call-descriptor\n1108\t  \"Admit a descriptor constructed by trusted UAST/profile code. This is not\n1109\t   a source form: entry-spelled source maps never pass through this constructor.\"\n1110\t  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n1111\t  (let [descriptor-name 'dsg__descriptor\n1112\t        canonical (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) descriptor-ast\n1113\t                         (u/lit :clj/admission) (u/lit nil))\n1114\t        ;; The factory closure captures the canonical descriptor and private"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_KI9gOTw13FpHJL46GDaC2765","content":"3500\tcells.\n3501\t\n3502\tRust requires ownership and lifetime analysis beyond parsing, plus\n3503\texplicit drop behavior. Those analyses may be an additional service\n3504\tstage without changing the frontend SPI.\n3505\t\n3506\tRaw native pointers are host capabilities, never portable literals.\n3507\tUnsafe/native operations need a separately declared profile.\n3508\t\n3509\tC preprocessing, Rust macro expansion, SQL dialect resolution, TypeScript\n3510\tchecking, and Ruby dynamic dispatch are plugin-owned stages. Each has\n3511\texplicit inputs, outputs, and dependencies. None requires Yang core to\n3512\trecognize its language by name.\n3513\t\n3514\t### 8.10 Shared function calling convention\n3515\t\n3516\t**Status: proposed, 2026-10-29; not implemented.** This section specifies\n3517\tone invocation convention for every conforming ANTLR-based Yang frontend.\n3518\tExamples are non-exhaustive. Adding a language must not add a case to Yang\n3519\tcore, a language-pair bridge, or an evaluator transition. The words\n3520\t**must**, **must not**, and **may** state requirements on a future\n3521\tconforming implementation, not claims about current code.\n3522\t\n3523\t#### 8.10.1 Decision and scope\n3524\t\n3525\tA Yin function is a Yin function, independent of its source syntax. The\n3526\tVM applies a closure to operands. Source calling semantics are ordinary\n3527\tUAST implementing the call site and callee entry, above the VM.\n3528\t\n3529\tEvery supported source-level callable, after its source-required\n3530\tresolution, exposes `:yang.call/entry`, an ordinary Yin closure taking\n3531\texactly one invocation record. Invoking it is an ordinary\n3532\t`:application`. No AST tag, lambda slot, instruction, host primitive,\n3533\teffect kind, or source-language test is added to the VM.\n3534\t\n3535\tThis is an internal calling convention, not a transport, another system\n3536\tABI, or a host callback interface. Calls between source languages inside\n3537\tone task do not themselves cross a host boundary. Portable I/O and\n3538\tcross-task interaction continue through `dao.stream`.\n3539\t\n3540\t**Transparent calling** means that an admitted callable can be passed,\n3541\tstored, returned, and invoked by any conforming frontend without a\n3542\thandwritten language-pair wrapper. It does not mean every foreign value\n3543\tsatisfies every source operation. Invocation, name visibility, and value\n3544\tinterpretation are distinct obligations.\n3545\t\n3546\tThe convention covers ordinary source calls and supported callable\n3547\tobjects, including higher-order calls. It does not make macros runtime\n3548\tfunctions, grant JavaScript `[[Construct]]`, turn a generator into an\n3549\tordinary returning function, or add a source feature a frontend refuses.\n3550\tConstructors and asynchronous operations keep their declared source\n3551\tsemantics; ordinary callability does not imply either capability.\n3552\t\n3553\t#### 8.10.2 Callable representation and identity\n3554\t\n3555\tKeep the callable's existing identity and source-specific data. Add the\n3556\tcommon entry beside its private code and metadata:\n3557\t\n3558\t```clojure\n3559\t;; Illustrative contents of one task-owned Python function cell.\n3560\t;; `entry` and `body-code` are live Yin closures, not literal AST maps.\n3561\t{:yang.call/entry entry\n3562\t :py/type :function\n3563\t :spec parameter-spec\n3564\t :defaults defaults\n3565\t :code body-code}\n3566\t```\n3567\t\n3568\tThe existing `:code` field is not the shared entry: its signature differs\n3569\tbetween preludes. It may remain private. Cross-language callers must not\n3570\tinspect it or extract it to bypass the entry.\n3571\t\n3572\tA cell-backed callable stores the entry in its cell contents. An\n3573\timmutable callable descriptor, such as a bound method, may carry it\n3574\tdirectly in its map. The common prelude projects the entry structurally:\n3575\tread an existing sealed cell reference through `cell/get`, or inspect\n3576\tthe immutable descriptor, then obtain `:yang.call/entry`. It must not\n3577\tdispatch on `:py/type`, `:js/type`, `:php/type`, language names, or a\n3578\tregistry of languages.\n3579\t\n3580\tAn admitted callable is a runtime cell/descriptor constructed or exposed\n3581\tby the callable constructors or import/export projections of a pinned,\n3582\tconforming profile. The entry slot is a runtime descriptor field, not a\n3583\tsource property that promotes arbitrary data to a function. A Python\n3584\tdictionary, JavaScript object, or PHP array containing a source key\n3585\tspelled `:yang.call/entry` remains ordinary source data unless an explicit\n3586\tprofile-defined projection makes it a callable descriptor. Source\n3587\tproperty access must not overwrite or masquerade as this runtime slot.\n3588\tThis is an obligation of construction and source resolution, not a new\n3589\tVM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\n3590\tthe resolved descriptor is admitted, the shared projection is structural;\n3591\tUAST deliberately constructing a conforming descriptor opts into the\n3592\tconvention rather than changing a source language's data-map semantics.\n3593\t\n3594\tMissing entry means not callable. Constructors must install a genuine\n3595\tunary Yin closure, and supported source mutations must preserve that\n3596\tinvariant. Unary arity is a constructor/profile conformance obligation,\n3597\tnot a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\n3598\tVM's existing argument binding does not enforce this convention's arity.\n3599\tA key in a map grants no VM privilege; application, ownership, and\n3600\teffect checks still apply. A non-applicable entry remains an operational\n3601\tVM application defect, not a source exception caught by the shared helper.\n3602\t\n3603\tFor callable kinds whose eligibility can change, the same cell or\n3604\tdescriptor may also contain `:yang.call/eligible?`, a unary Yin predicate\n3605\ton the original callable. Without it, an entry is eligible by default.\n3606\tWith it, the common callable test uses its boolean result. The predicate\n3607\treads explicit runtime metadata/heap only; it must not mutate state,\n3608\tevaluate arguments, execute the target body, or invoke getters/user hooks.\n3609\tIt has the same constructor/arity obligations as the entry. For example,"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"**Do not ACCEPT as implemented.** The static `intra-unit-fn?` eligibility analysis is suitably conservative, but the implementation introduces a public call-entry escape hatch.\n\n`yang.call/entry` is specified as an **ordinary Yin closure taking exactly one invocation record** (`docs/design/yang.antlr.md:3529-3533`, `:3594-3598`). The fix instead publishes a two-parameter closure whose guest-controlled second argument selects the private lane (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1055-1104`).\n\nA guest can extract that public closure and invoke it with a truthy second argument:\n\n```clojure\n(defn f [x] x)\n(let [raw (yang.call/entry f)\n      v [raw]]\n  (raw [42] true))\n```\n\nThis returns the body’s raw outcome (`[:ok 42]`) rather than the ordinary call value `42`. For a throwing function, it can similarly expose the raw error outcome instead of performing public outcome-to-raise conversion. Existing tests already establish that guests can project and invoke the raw entry (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2296-2322`), so this is reachable without forging a descriptor or defeating `intra-unit-fn?`.\n\nThe direct lane therefore needs to be **unavailable through the published unary entry**: use a separately stored private body/entry or an unforgeable direct-call capability. A truthy positional flag is not authentication.\n\nWithin the reviewed scope, the static routing itself handles shadowing, `def`/`defn` interactions, forward references, and repeated definitions conservatively; I found no separate static-eligibility escape. The unchanged budget and lack of diagnostic coverage credit are respected. The reported gate results are seat-supplied and otherwise satisfy the requested quality gate."}
